Z||000001||Archie||08-22-2001||08:56 PM||||Wow, looks like I've missed a lot of posts. I've been a little out of touch since last Thursday. I've been here but didn't have too much time to read long winded threads  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I don't have Pat's contact info handy but I can tell you where he got the transmission. First, I have to tell you about the car I'm just finishing up..... It's a 1988 Coupe and we've installed a 450+HP SBC engine With Dual Quads and an automatic (Built by the same guy). The inspiration comes from Pat's car and this car is ment for drag racing only.<P>We will be test driving it before the weekend and I'll be adding NOS after a few test runs at the strip. I'm positive that this car will also be in the 10's.<P>The guy who has been building all of these beefed-up 125's is Jim Paquet owner of JPT Transmissions,  Eaton Rapids, MI 517-663-0578.<P>Archie||||reg||1
